# The Vercel CLI uploads the entire cwd (repo root) and only honors .vercelignore
# (NOT .gitignore). The project's Root Directory is `wrench_deploy`, so deploys must
# run from the repo root — but we only need to upload wrench_deploy/ itself.
# Without this file the CLI uploads ~4.9 GB of root-level DBs/caches/backups and
# fails the 100 MB per-file limit (complaints_api_cache.json, wrench_vehicles.db).

# Ignore everything at the repo root...
/*
# ...except the deploy root.
!/wrench_deploy

# Within the deploy root, drop backups and local node_modules (Vercel reinstalls deps).
wrench_deploy/*.bak
wrench_deploy/*.bak*
wrench_deploy/**/*.bak
wrench_deploy/**/*.bak*
wrench_deploy/node_modules

# Hobby plan caps a deployment at 12 Serverless Functions; api/ has 13.
# obd.py is a stub that can't work in the cloud (OBD-II needs the local
# wrench_serve.py + a physical ELM327 adapter), so it's excluded here.
# The client's fetch().catch() already shows the correct "run it locally" message.
wrench_deploy/api/obd.py
